# 08 — K10-R7-01 distinguishing demonstration, clean payload C

Two readers over one document. H7 is the reviewed candidate
2dfc6d818498263c30cb64db32a91aa0ac0543a5's inventory-oracle.ts, taken byte-for-byte with
`git show`; its two imports are `import type` and are erased by --experimental-strip-types,
so the copy runs standalone and is the reviewed code, not a paraphrase of it. C is the
committed production parser, imported from its real path in the payload tree. Every case is
the real ownership inventory with one mutation, read through inventoryDisagreements plus
parseDependencyTable — the same end-to-end path C4 asserts on.

$ git show 2dfc6d818498263c30cb64db32a91aa0ac0543a5:tests/conformance/architecture/inventory-oracle.ts | shasum -a 256
e919b7289e7e4f3da3f0f0da3825e2ab6cff065e94d17ff8d2757dc4649fe813  -

The H7 lines this demonstration turns on:

```ts
function sectionText(markdown: string, heading: string, nextHeading: string): string {
  const from = markdown.indexOf(heading);
  if (from === -1) return "";
  const rest = markdown.slice(from + heading.length);
  const to = rest.indexOf(nextHeading);
  return to === -1 ? rest : rest.slice(0, to);
}
```

with H7 call sites using loose textual prefixes:

```ts
sectionTables(markdown, "## Zones", "## Current cross-boundary"),
sectionTables(markdown, "## Deferred extraction", "## What this packet"),
sectionTables(markdown, "## Export ownership", "## What the target zone may import"),
sectionTables(markdown, "## Current cross-boundary", "## Export ownership"),
```

and their replacements in C — a block scanner over exact titles:

```ts
function sectionLines(markdown: string, currentTitle: string, nextTitle: string): string[]
// start: first level-2 ATX heading outside fenced code with text === currentTitle
// end:   first later level-2 ATX heading outside fenced code with text === nextTitle

sectionTables(markdown, "Zones", "Current cross-boundary dependencies"),
sectionTables(markdown, "Deferred extraction and bridge owners", "What this packet does not establish"),
sectionTables(markdown, "Export ownership", "What the target zone may import"),
sectionTables(markdown, "Current cross-boundary dependencies", "Export ownership"),
```

supported by `parseAtxHeading` (≤3 spaces indent, 1–6 `#`, required whitespace/EOL,
closing-sequence strip, no blockquote), `parseFenceCandidate` (matched char/length, backtick
info rule) and `updateFence` (a mismatched closer does not exit).

