## Reading 08 — what this shows

- The review-07 literal is silent under H7 (0 messages) and reported under C (2 rows). The
  fenced-code shape behaves identically. Both are the same defect class: the section end was a
  substring, found before any Markdown context could be consulted.
- SELF-15 (`##Current…`, no required whitespace) reports under both readers: H7's substring
  happens to require the space, so it never truncated there. It is committed as a control anyway
  because a future prefix-stripping parser could reopen it; structural recognition settles it.
- The prose-start case shows the other direction of the same defect: H7 selects the section at
  prose bytes (9 false messages about a planted table that is not in the section), while C stays
  green by waiting for the real ATX heading.
- SELF-12, SELF-13 and the K10-R6-01 header-label case report under both readers: the round-7
  repair is preserved verbatim by the committed suite (16 header-label variants plus the
  repeated-heading, further-table, renamed-header and missing-table controls, all still passing
  in 03/04).
